# Create virtual environment
python -m venv .venv

# Activate it
.venv\Scripts\activate

# Install all project dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Install Playwright browser binaries
playwright install

# Run tests
pytest

# install all browsers
playwright install

# Or install only Chromium:
playwright install chromium


# Verify the installation
pip list

# or check a specific package:

pip show playwright

# delete file
rmdir filename/folder

# install playwright 

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv .venv

# Activate it
.venv\Scripts\activate

# Upgrade pip
python -m pip install --upgrade pip

# Install Playwright
pip install playwright

# Install browser binaries
playwright install

# Install pytest (optional but recommended)
pip install pytest pytest-playwright


# how to run tests

Run a single test file (Recommended)
pytest tests/login.py

or

python -m pytest tests/login.py
4. Run all tests
pytest

or

pytest tests
5. Run with verbose output
pytest -v tests/login.py

Example output:

============================= test session starts =============================

tests/login.py::test_valid_login PASSED
tests/login.py::test_invalid_login PASSED

======================== 2 passed in 6.24s ========================
6. Run a specific test function

Suppose login.py contains:

def test_valid_login():
    ...

def test_invalid_login():
    ...

Run only one test:

pytest tests/login.py::test_valid_login
7. Show browser while running

If your test launches the browser with:

browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=False)

then run normally:

pytest tests/login.py

If your code uses a headless option controlled by configuration, make sure it's set to False to see the browser.

8. Run tests in paralle
Install:

pip install pytest-xdist

Run:

pytest -n 4

9. Generate an HTML report (after installing pytest-html)

Install:

pip install pytest-html

Run:

pytest --html=report.html
10. Run with console logs
pytest -v -s tests/login.py
-v = verbose output
-s = shows print() output in the console

# Common pytest commands

| Command                                   | Purpose                                                                               |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `pytest`                                  | Run all tests                                                                         |
| `pytest tests`                            | Run all tests in the `tests` folder                                                   |
| `pytest tests/login.py`                   | Run one test file                                                                     |
| `pytest tests/login.py::test_valid_login` | Run one test function                                                                 |
| `pytest -v`                               | Verbose output                                                                        |
| `pytest -s`                               | Show `print()` statements                                                             |
| `pytest -v -s`                            | Verbose + show console output                                                         |
| `pytest -k login`                         | Run tests whose names match `login`                                                   |
| `pytest -m smoke`                         | Run tests marked with `@pytest.mark.smoke`                                            |
| `pytest --headed`                         | Run Playwright tests with a visible browser (when using the Playwright pytest plugin) |
| `pytest --browser chromium`               | Run tests in Chromium (with the Playwright pytest plugin)                             |
| `pytest --browser firefox`                | Run tests in Firefox (with the Playwright pytest plugin)                              |
| `pytest --browser webkit`                 | Run tests in WebKit (with the Playwright pytest plugin)                               |
